+# Exact finite full-four-dimensional local connection sheet
+
+SOURCE #310. Input `61688727ab3273bf35318f10ca789937b0b8f9b3`.
+[Proof and exact scope](sources/d0_full_four_dimensional_sheet_2026-10-15/RESULT_RU.md).
+
+A directed-interval Banach certificate constructs an exact 384-variable
+(two-coordinate) curved root of the unchanged naked-star action on L=4.
+Translation symmetry proves all 6144 local connection rows vanish. Crucially,
+ALL sixteen transverse Bloch blocks of its full 6144-dimensional Hessian
+are interval-invertible, with full inverse bound <2^24. The implicit-function
+theorem therefore supplies an open neighbourhood of arbitrary 4096-component
+four-dimensional coframe data with unique nearby exact connection roots.
+The new coframes and roots are not restricted to a coordinate ansatz.
+Full source derivatives have the actual on-shell Schur formula.
+
+This is a finite open curved connection sheet, not a uniform L->infinity
+estimate, prescribed-source metric/matter solve, stable energy minimum,
+full Cost-Info binding, or GR closure. The severe finite inverse constant is
+reported, not suppressed. No previous task/claim/BOOK status is changed.
+
+The new interval kernel independently copies endpoint arrays. The upstream
+one-coordinate kernel's np.asarray alias bug is reproduced; a separate
+minimal repair patch is included, but the old L=8 interval receipt is not
+silently refreshed. Its analytic one-coordinate theorem is unaffected.
+
+New proof replay requires NumPy, SymPy and mpmath. The optional JAX full-6144
+row test is a labelled numerical diagnostic only. No new Lean compilation
+or whole-repository CI pass is claimed. This intake has not yet been pushed.
